      "confidence": "high",
      "marks_pos": 1.0,
      "marks_neg": 0.25,
      "question": "Which of the following two signs need to be interchanged to make the given equation correct?\n\n72 div 12 - 7 + 9 times 36 = 15",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "1",
          "text": "+ and -"
        },
        {
          "label": "2",
          "text": "× and -"
        },
        {
          "label": "3",
          "text": "+and÷"
        },
        {
          "label": "4",
          "text": "÷ and ×"
        }
      ],
      "correct": "2",
      "solution": "BODMAS Table: \n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/7751840ca1840d12cadc428f84d30e2cdcd5e7f82d52a57de21f2404c58eed88.png] \n\nGiven equation: 72÷12−7+9×36=15 \n\nNow, if ‘+’ and ‘-‘ and ‘×' and '÷’ are interchanged, then:\n\nOption 1) + and -\n\n72 ÷ 12 + 7 − 9 × 36\n\n72 ÷ 12 = 6\n9 × 36 = 324\n\n \n\n6 + 7 − 324 = **−311**\n\nOption 2) **× and -**\n\n**72 ÷ 12 × 7 + 9 − 36**\n\n**72 ÷ 12 = 6\n6 × 7 = 42**\n\n \n\n**42 + 9 − 36 = ****15**\n\nOption 3) + and ÷\n\n72 + 12 − 7 ÷ 9 × 36\n\n7 ÷ 9 × 36 = 28\n\n \n\n72 + 12 − 28 = **56**\n\nOption 4) ÷ and ×\n\n72 × 12 − 7 + 9 ÷ 36\n\n72 × 12 = 864\n9 ÷ 36 = 0.25\n\n \n\n864 − 7 + 0.25 = **857.25**\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option 2\".",
      "solution_images": [
        {
          "url": "https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/7751840ca1840d12cadc428f84d30e2cdcd5e7f82d52a57de21f2404c58eed88.png",
          "alt": ""
        }
      ],
      "tags": [
        "Logical Puzzle"
      ]
    },
